sp.p:
Well, you see there are three of us, at any rate, who could have done no
                            better than come here and make one household of it. As for the fourth;
                            as for Clara—

I'm not certain, sir. Sometimes I think it was natural perversity;
                            sometimes I think it was false pride at getting over sea-sickness;
                            sometimes I think it was reading “Robinson Crusoe,” and books warning of
                            me not to go to sea.
